{"id":"2000982862988603503","kind":"article","title":"Execute Program 的课程相当短","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zLnMMGiCT6xDjMfMurTzKjs"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"助记媒介 & 思想工具","date":"2026-01-31","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":2,"comment_count":2,"minutes":1,"chars":615,"keywords":["Execute Program","交互式学习","助记媒介","情景体验","编程教育"],"summary":"作者观察到 Execute Program 的课程通常只有几分钟：简短解释后立即操作，再通过交互卡片重复练习关键概念。他认为，读者能在体验中理解内容，使课程无需冗长讲解；这种短小、按互动展开的结构类似复习环节，也可视为情景体验或可执行书籍的初步形式。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2000982862988603503","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"pHwTTKnZ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zSsjk5UvNPGrYp8B6DEFCMS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program</a> 的课程通常只有几分钟。你会读几段关于新概念的文字，立刻上手尝试，然后重复几次，以覆盖该概念的一些核心细节。然后就结束了。</p><p data-pid=\"-DLatjLV\">这种简短在一定程度上是因为 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zH26uarYCm9y6tqzuxaGUzt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>，但我感觉交互式卡片的存在起了更大的作用。作者不需要花太多时间描述概念，因为读者马上就会亲身体验它。这与我写过的几个现象有关：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"z2Q4xef3\">它是对一种<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z92TGMiBsnraf5KXxSTNkBJ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">情景体验</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>的非常粗略的近似</li><ul><li data-pid=\"sGaLa8BG\">（尤其是<a class=\"wrap external\" data-draft-title=\"情景体验可以引导人们积极参与到赋能环境中\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zKubRcJXKjiCDPsPgJWckkP\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">情景体验可以引导人们积极参与到赋能环境中</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>）</li></ul><li data-pid=\"ld1N4F0E\">在<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zLNcy2JiH3AGNaZjYkHzK9P\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可执行书籍</a>中也有类似效果</li><li data-pid=\"ZqHgc4TO\">在<a class=\"wrap external\" data-draft-title=\"助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zTzb8spnoqzxs3mkvPKprmn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>所描述的一些影响</li></ul><p data-pid=\"TStieYlB\">因此，这些课程在体验上其实很像复习环节：你可以在一次短暂的坐下来把它完成，并且它不会过度消耗你的注意力。课程与复习环节之间这种相似性，又会被两者交互模型的相似性进一步放大：<a class=\"wrap external\" data-draft-title=\"Execute Program 的课程根据读者的互动逐段展开正文\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zWeMGj1huQaESSBTmRWSvD5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program 的课程根据读者的互动逐段展开正文</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"VtO5xpBC\">另见：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zHwr5v9VJGX3MzHyzz4V8wt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">渐进阅读</a></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"gVa5JIkT\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"576613520\" href=\"#/post/576613520\">助记文本可以在一段时间内分小段连载，根据读者的记忆情况排期</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"a1kSLiu9\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"LmxKl2KQ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 gpt-5.2-high，校对 Jarrett Ye<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zLnMMGiCT6xDjMfMurTzKjs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program’s lessons are quite short</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"2001689461378012509\" href=\"#/post/2001689461378012509\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 情景体验（Enacted experience） <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"463926133\" href=\"#/post/463926133\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 情景体验可以引导人们积极参与到赋能环境中 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"654019484\" href=\"#/post/654019484\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"463608296\" href=\"#/post/463608296\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> Execute Program 的课程根据读者的互动逐段展开正文 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1999145478621769990\" href=\"#/post/1999145478621769990\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"2000259693428351079","title":"Execute Program 的卡片既是应用卡片，也是回忆卡片","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":6,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"2001372387644563990","title":"在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":9,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"2001689461378012509","title":"Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":3,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"1999145478621769990","title":"Execute Program 的课程根据读者的互动逐段展开正文","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":6,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"463608296","title":"助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":6,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[]}